  "result": "Excellent! All 193 tests pass. I've successfully added credit note functionality:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n   - CREDIT_TOO_HIGH - when credit amount exceeds invoice total\n\n2. **src/credits.js** (new module):\n   - `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` function\n   - Accepts invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n   - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n   - Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n   - Returns ok(creditNote) with: { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n   - Credit notes numbered CN-<year>-<counter> (separate counter from invoices)\n   - Handles both INV-... and CN-... numbers in existingNumbers\n   - Separate counters per year\n   - Helper function `nextCreditNoteNumber()` mirrors invoice numbering structure\n\n3. **test/credits.test.js** - 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Creating credit notes for different invoice statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n   - Rejection of draft invoices\n   - Amount validation (positive integer only)\n   - Credit limits (cannot exceed invoice total)\n   - Separate numbering from invoices\n   - Counter incrementing across notes\n   - Year-based counter separation\n   - Data preservation (invoice number, customer ID)\n\n**Key design**: Credit notes are independent numbered documents (CN prefix) representing refunds on already-issued invoices, with separate year-based counters from invoices.",
